	(footprint "SOT-23-6_SP3019_LittelfuseLand"
		(layer "F.Cu")
		(uuid "e45a5234-de75-4515-9876-ec56b324f378")
		(at 115.6 97.1 -90)
		(descr "SOT23-6L with the land pattern Littelfuse recommends for the SP3019 / SP3012-04HTG: pads 0.60 x 0.85, 0.95 pitch, 3.33 overall (the drawing prints this span as 0.33, a digit cut off; read as 3.33, the only reading that fits the package table's 2.60 to 3.00 mm lead span with pads 0.85 mm long: 0.33 would put the pads inside the leads) (hardware/datasheets/SP3019_littelfuse_rev2018-01-25.pdf page 5, Recommended soldering pad layout). The KiCad SOT-23-6 pads are 1.325 long and leave a 0.95 channel between the two pad rows; this one leaves 1.63 mm, which two 90 ohm lines need to pass between the rows.")
